  ],
  "notes": "Two parallel failure paths converge on the same consequence: (1) a material/hardening defect causing wear-driven loss of CRACS Train A's 30-day mission capability, discovered retroactively via engineering review after a parts-issue notice from Carrier; (2) planned EDG Train B maintenance triggering TS 3.8.1 Required Action B.2, which required CRACS Train B (support-system relationship) to also be declared inoperable, even though it remained physically capable (offsite power available). The event was reported under 50.73(a)(2)(i)(B) for the prohibited-condition/LCO 3.0.3 violation; NUREG-1022 guidance cited to explain why 50.73(a)(2)(v) does NOT apply (single-failure-assumption carve-out), but the field code lists both criteria, so both are recorded as REPORTED_UNDER per the authoritative FORM-366 field. Previous similar event (May 26, 2024 CRACS Train B failure) is described only narratively without a formal LER number, so a stub LER node uses a placeholder key; downstream resolver should treat with caution given no true LER number was stated in text (only a date-described event). System GK/CMP/C008 codes taken verbatim from block 13; EIIS bracket code for CRACS/CREVS in text reads '[EIIS:VI]' (interpreted as VI, though may be a scanning artifact of 'VI' due to OCR — copied literally as given)."
